 ### Labelmap Transfer Function LUT Construction
-Constructs two 1D LUT textures (soft and hard) for labelmap transfer functions [S3, unofficial]. The soft LUT uses float precision and bilinear filtering; the hard LUT uses byte precision and point filtering [S3, unofficial]. It initializes arrays, maps label indices to LUT entries, converts float colors to byte, and uploads to GPU textures [S3, unofficial]. The LUT size is constant 256 [S3, unofficial].
+Constructs two 1D LUT textures (soft and hard) for labelmap transfer functions. The soft LUT uses float precision and bilinear filtering; the hard LUT uses byte precision and point filtering [S3, unofficial]. Initializes floatPixels array of size 256 with Color(0,0,0,0) and bytePixels array of size 256 with Color32(0,0,0,0) [S3, unofficial]. If data.tf.entries is not null, iterates over each entry e. Calculates idx as Mathf.Clamp(Mathf.RoundToInt(e.label), 0, lutSize-1). Extracts r, g, b from e.color (default 0f) and a from e.alpha. Stores in floatPixels[idx] [S3, unofficial]. Converts r, g, b, a from float [0,1] to byte [0,255] by multiplying by 255, rounding, and clamping to [0,255]. Stores in bytePixels[idx] [S3, unofficial]. Creates lutSoft as Texture2D(lutSize, 1, RGBAFloat, false). Sets wrapMode Clamp, filterMode Bilinear. Sets pixels from floatPixels and applies [S3, unofficial]. Creates lutHard as Texture2D(lutSize, 1, RGBA32, false). Sets wrapMode Clamp, filterMode Point. Sets pixels32 from bytePixels and applies [S3, unofficial]. Assigns lutSoft to data.tfLUTTextureSoft and lutHard to data.tfLUTTextureHard [S3, unofficial]. Parameter: lutSize is a constant integer value 256, representing the maximum number of labels [S3, unofficial].
